---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { repoFile } from "../config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="Servotab project status, website rights boundary, and layered source licensing context."
>
  <PageIntro
    index="06 / Terms"
    title="Terms follow the material you receive."
    description="This page states the website and identity boundary. Any source package is governed by the licensing files distributed with that package."
  />

  <article class="legal-document shell">
    <div class="legal-grid">
      <aside class="legal-aside">Last updated<br />31 August 2026</aside>
      <div class="legal-prose">
        <section>
          <h2>Project status and affiliation</h2>
          <p>
            Servotab is an independent, community-maintained project. It is not an
            official OpenAI product, is not currently listed in the OpenAI plugin
            directory, and this website does not represent directory approval or availability.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Source-package licensing</h2>
          <p>
            The public Servotab repository contains the current source candidate; it is
            not a tagged release or an OpenAI directory publication. The path-level{" "}
            <a href={repoFile("LICENSING.md")}>licensing map</a>, governing license texts,
            package-local notices, and third-party terms shipped with those exact files
            control. Repository access does not collapse those layers into one license.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Functional materials</h2>
          <p>
            Project-original functional materials expressly identified by the current
            map—including methods, scripts, the generated skill projection, manifests,
            and behavior fixtures—are governed by the{" "}
            <a href={repoFile("LICENSE")}>Sustainable Use License v1.0</a>. Public source
            visibility does not expand that license or turn the repository into an OSI
            open-source distribution.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Documentation</h2>
          <p>
            Project-original expression in the documentation paths specifically identified
            by the current map is governed by{" "}
            <a href={repoFile("LICENSE-DOCUMENTATION.md")}>CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>.
            That license does not automatically apply to this website, identity assets,
            functional source, methods, scripts, manifests, fixtures, or other materials.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Third-party material and earlier revisions</h2>
          <p>
            Third-party material, names, terminology, and notices remain under their
            respective rights and licenses. Historical attribution is recorded in the{" "}
            <a href={repoFile("THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md")}>Third-Party Notices</a>, and
            the earlier forward-only boundary is recorded in{" "}
            <a href={repoFile("LICENSE-HISTORY.md")}>License History</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Website and identity</h2>
          <p>
            The Servotab name, mark, raster identity exports, and original prose and
            visual compositions on this website are not offered for third-party reuse.
            Their public visibility does not create a trademark, copyright, or reuse grant.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Current product information</h2>
          <p>
            Pages on this site describe the current public product model, source-candidate
            availability, website, and release status. The Servotab repository is the current
            source authority and preserves the earlier Softpowers commits, release records,
            and provenance. Source-checkout installation remains distinct from a tagged
            release, OpenAI directory submission, directory publication, and OpenAI approval.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
